Subject: Bridge kubectl and client-go TerminalSizeQueue after k8s v0.36 decoupling

Origin: DHI-internal (Kubernetes client compatibility)
Description: Adapt term.MonitorSize output to remotecommand.TerminalSizeQueue after kubectl and client-go types diverged.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/loft-sh/devspace.git 7f272dcf90653fa9b42bc4347f7f3f9a52b0e8b5
Verify: test alpine-3.23/6.yaml
Forwarded: not-needed (DevSpace 6.3.x has not merged kubectl v0.36 terminal queue types)
Drop-When: never: loft-sh/devspace v6.3.21 still assigns MonitorSize without a client-go bridge; drop after upstream merges kubectl v0.36 terminal queue adapter

k8s.io/kubectl and k8s.io/client-go now expose distinct TerminalSizeQueue interfaces with identical method shapes. DevSpace pod exec must bridge MonitorSize output when DHI aligns Kubernetes module versions alongside the buildkit bump on DevSpace 6.3.21.

diff --git a/pkg/devspace/kubectl/exec.go b/pkg/devspace/kubectl/exec.go
--- a/pkg/devspace/kubectl/exec.go
+++ b/pkg/devspace/kubectl/exec.go
@@ -25,6 +25,22 @@ const (
 	SubResourceAttach SubResource = "attach"
 )
 
+type termTerminalSizeQueueAdapter struct {
+	inner term.TerminalSizeQueue
+}
+
+func (a *termTerminalSizeQueueAdapter) Next() *remotecommand.TerminalSize {
+	size := a.inner.Next()
+	if size == nil {
+		return nil
+	}
+	return &remotecommand.TerminalSize{
+		Width:  size.Width,
+		Height: size.Height,
+	}
+}
+
